Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 346/488] soh: name the 15 address-named symbols defined in
 z_bg_spot01_idohashira.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 15 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Spot01_Idohashira/z_bg_spot01_idohashira.c.

  * func_808AAD3C -> BgSpot01Idohashira_SpawnSpark
    deduced, confidence HIGH: fills in an EffectSparkInit at the given point
    with black start colours and the caller's UV division, and adds it.

  * func_808AAE6C -> BgSpot01Idohashira_SpawnBreakEffects
    deduced, confidence HIGH: throws the large dust cloud and spark burst at
    the arch's position and plays the breaking sfx.

  * func_808AAF34 -> BgSpot01Idohashira_SpawnPostEffects
    deduced, confidence HIGH: while the arch is falling, throws a smaller
    dust cloud and spark burst at each of its two posts, transformed into
    world space by the current matrix.

  * func_808AB18C -> BgSpot01Idohashira_Tumble
    deduced, confidence HIGH: adds the per-axis tumble rates to the arch's
    rotation each frame while it falls.

  * func_808AB1DC -> BgSpot01Idohashira_GetFreeFallY
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the osSyncPrintf in its divide-by-zero guard
    names it "Bg_Spot01_Idohashira_Get_FreeFall"; it returns the height
    along a parabola between the start and end heights for the given frame.

  * func_808AB29C -> BgSpot01Idohashira_FollowFallPath
    deduced, confidence HIGH: interpolates the arch along the cue's start
    and end positions with that free-fall curve for the height, and returns
    true once it lands.

  * func_808AB3E8 -> BgSpot01Idohashira_SetupStanding
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the cue-1 handler: sets the standing action
    and draw config.

  * func_808AB3F8 -> BgSpot01Idohashira_SetupFalling
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the cue-2 handler: sets the falling action and
    turns the post effects on.

  * func_808AB414 -> BgSpot01Idohashira_SetupLanded
    deduced, confidence HIGH: throws the break effects and switches to the
    landed action.

  * func_808AB444 -> BgSpot01Idohashira_CheckCue
    deduced, confidence HIGH: watches actor cue 2 and, when it changes,
    dispatches to the standing or falling setup.

  * func_808AB504 -> BgSpot01Idohashira_DoNothing
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the empty action used before the cutscene
    starts and after the arch has landed.

  * func_808AB510 -> BgSpot01Idohashira_Standing
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the standing action: it does nothing but watch
    for the next cue.

  * func_808AB530 -> BgSpot01Idohashira_Falling
    deduced, confidence HIGH: tumbles the arch along its fall path and
    switches to the landed setup on arrival.

  * func_808AB570 -> BgSpot01Idohashira_Landed
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the settled action: it keeps watching the cue
    in case the cutscene resets it.

  * func_808AB700 -> BgSpot01Idohashira_DrawArch
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draws gKakarikoWellArchDL, spawning the
    falling post effects from inside the same matrix.

